\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:
It is assumed that extra rules will be written one day for verbs like 
{\em owe\/} (in the meaning: to have to pay - schuldig zijn)
and {\em teach\/}, that normally do not take a Prepobj and hence would give
no translation at all here, but that do allow a to-obj when the direct object 
is the perspro {\em it\/}: \\
? I owe a certain amount to him - I owe it to him\\
$^{*}$I taught the lesson to them - I taught it to them\\
These extra rules are possible only if these verbs receive a special synpattern 
to indicate this option.
For verbs that do not have this possibility, like {\em allow\/} and {\em permit
\/}, no solution has been found yet, and therefore, no translation will be 
given for the Dutch sentence {\em Ik heb het hun toegestaan\/}
\end{enumerate}
